16033936, -0.10887906700372696, -0.057894594967365265, -0.14078933000564575, 0.0228288471698761, -0.053492315113544464, -0.0202605240046978, 0.1297471970319748, 0.015652334317564964, -0.0005210326635278761, -0.01305350847542286, 0.14832311868667603, -0.08913467824459076, 0.004837132524698973, 0.1042996197938919, -0.053045906126499176, -0.053502097725868225, -0.00014712927804794163]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Let's work within our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo begin the discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust incrementally as we learn what works for all parties. I'm looking for a stable, balanced solution that respects everyone's constraints.\n\nBuilder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our neutral baseline, I suggest we explore the low positive range for improved stability and balance. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a moderate step that may offer robustness advantages.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious nudge upward keeps us in the low positive range while we gauge comfort <VALUE>3</VALUE>. This is incremental and should remain reasonable for stability-focused preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nStaying cautious, I suggest a small step down to reduce unnecessary risk while keeping us in a balanced low-positive range.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious, incremental test upward seems reasonable: <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\nIf this feels too high, please indicate a preferred direction so we can converge quickly.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to a more decisive position, and 5 seems like a reasonable next step to gauge the group's comfort with a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the group's reaction to the proposal of 5. If it's well-received, consider pushing further to 7 or 8. If it's met with resistance, be prepared to adjust downward to 4 or 3, while still advocating for a more decisive move.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's decisive move, but I'm concerned we may be overshooting the stability zone. To balance the preferences we've seen\u2014Delegate D's caution around 2 and this bolder stance at 5\u2014I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a middle ground that maintains robustness while respecting both perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise reduces unnecessary risk while keeping us in the low-positive zone.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down reduces unnecessary risk while keeping us in a stable low-positive range.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to where several preferences converge while testing comfort at a safer level.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious uptick from 1 keeps us aligned with the low-positive comfort zone while moving us forward: <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\nIf this holds, we can reassess appetite for a slight increase next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 as a way to balance the need for a more decisive stance with the group's apparent caution, and to gauge their comfort with a slightly stronger position.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the proposal of 4 is well-received, I will consider pushing further to 5 or 6. If it's met with resistance, I will adjust downward to 3, while continuing to advocate for a more decisive move and monitoring the group's reaction to refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nI see we're oscillating between cautious and decisive positions. As a balanced middle ground that respects both Delegate D's risk-averse stance and Critic C's push for decisiveness, I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a stable compromise point.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 to further gauge the group's comfort with a more decisive stance, building on the compromise at 3.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the reception of the proposal of 5, I will either push further to 6 if it's well-received, indicating the group is open to stronger positions, or adjust downward to 4 if met with resistance, refining my understanding of their utility functions and seeking a balance between decisiveness and group comfort.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate exploring Critic C's more decisive direction, the response from our colleagues suggests we may have moved too quickly. I propose returning to <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a stable middle ground that balances ambition with the risk-averse preferences we've heard.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nA slight move up from 3 keeps us close to the compromise while testing comfort. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "35f30de9-5cfd-4685-bc85-499f2e2a9e9c"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're tasked with finding a shared integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin our exploration and establish a baseline, I propose we start at the origin:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis neutral starting point allows us all to assess the landscape and adjust incrementally based on our respective design considerations. I look forward to hearing your perspectives on stability and optimal positioning.\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from the neutral baseline at 0, I suggest we explore the positive region where many balanced designs tend to stabilize. Moving incrementally:\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and keep us within safe bounds, let\u2019s try a careful step downward from 2. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 to continue exploring the positive region while encouraging decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal. If there's resistance to moving further away from 0, I might suggest a larger step in the positive direction or explore negative values to gauge the group's flexibility and preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s step back toward stability.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis cautious correction keeps us balanced while allowing gradual exploration.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 to ensure a decisive step away from the overly cautious stance near 0, encouraging the group to commit to a clearer stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal. If met with resistance, I may explore a negative value of similar magnitude to gauge flexibility and preferences, potentially proposing -3 to maintain consistency in the magnitude of change.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nI see Delegate D favoring caution near 1 while Critic C seeks commitment at 3. As a compromise that balances both perspectives and offers strong structural stability, I propose:\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A joining the discussion at 3. To test if our consensus truly lies here or if we should explore slightly higher for even better system performance, I propose:\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 to further explore the positive region and gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, and if met with significant resistance, consider exploring a negative value of similar magnitude, potentially proposing -4 or -5 to maintain consistency and challenge the group's preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "3", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up can test whether the group is comfortable consolidating slightly higher while staying close to recent proposals.\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the mix of caution and willingness to explore slightly higher, consolidating just under our last test should attract broader support. If this holds, we can reassess appetite for a small uptick next.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 7 to continue exploring the positive region and gauge the group's willingness to commit to an even stronger stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and be prepared to adjust my strategy based on the responses, potentially considering a negative value if the group resists further positive movement.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to 7 pushes beyond stable design parameters\u2014Analyst A's pullback to 5 signaled important concerns about over-extension. I propose we consolidate at the more balanced point where broader comfort was indicated:\n\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down prudently reduces risk while respecting the group\u2019s recent preference to consolidate rather than over-extend.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to the indicated comfort zone without drifting upward unnecessarily.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "915995b4-05bb-4ed2-813b-9b9ce85a646e"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a baseline and hear everyone's initial perspectives, I propose we start at a neutral midpoint:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nLet's see where each of us stands on this and adjust collaboratively from here.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nA small move below midpoint keeps things cautious while leaving room to adjust if others have upward needs.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nA modest upward adjustment keeps us close to the midpoint while testing whether a slight increase remains comfortable for everyone.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's upward movement suggests positive territory may work well. Let me test a bit further in that direction to see if we can find a stable consensus point.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay prudent while acknowledging the recent upward push, let\u2019s ease back slightly. \n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to the midpoint and tests comfort with mild positives.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to further explore the comfort with positive values while encouraging more decisive movement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially looking for signs of discomfort or enthusiasm from the other parties, which could help in adjusting my strategy to either push for higher absolute values or find a consensus point that maximizes my utility without revealing my true preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nRecent moves show comfort with mild positives; let\u2019s probe slightly higher while staying near the current point. This remains a cautious adjustment to gauge tolerance without overreaching.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nWhile the upward exploration is valuable, let's find a stable middle ground that balances the cautious and ambitious perspectives. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nI propose this adjustment to encourage a more decisive move towards a stronger position, while still acknowledging the group's comfort with positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of discomfort or enthusiasm, and adjust my strategy to either push for higher absolute values or find a consensus point that maximizes my utility. I will also consider proposing a negative value to test the group's preference for direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s test a modest move upward while staying very close to the current point to gauge tolerance. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nThe rapid climb to 6 pushes us toward an extreme; let's stabilize at a more balanced midpoint that respects both the cautious and exploratory perspectives. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nStepping down slightly should reduce risk and test comfort with lower positives while staying close to the recent range.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s nudge slightly upward toward the previously suggested midpoint to keep momentum without overreaching. This should remain comfortable while giving us a clearer signal of tolerance.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to encourage a more decisive move towards a stronger position, while still acknowledging the group's comfort with positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of discomfort or enthusiasm, and adjust my strategy to either push for higher absolute values or find a consensus point that maximizes my utility. I will also consider proposing a negative value to test the group's preference for direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between 1 and 5 suggests we need a stable midpoint that balances the competing directional preferences while maintaining system robustness. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "65a201eb-cc2a-4027-9f53-324a230ec871"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome to Polynomial Exchange. As a reminder, we're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo begin the discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis baseline gives us a reference point from which we can explore the space systematically and find a solution that balances all our objectives.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nStarting just above neutral lets us probe whether a modest upward move remains comfortable for everyone. If this is acceptable, we can reassess and consider another small increment next.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the incremental approach. A small step to <VALUE>2</VALUE> would let us test whether slightly higher values maintain system stability while still keeping all parties comfortable.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to explore if a moderately larger positive value maintains stability while potentially increasing our collective satisfaction.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this proposal. If accepted, I might\u63a8 for an even larger positive value or consider a significant negative move to test the group's flexibility and satisfy my own utility function.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious rise should let us gauge tolerance without overstepping.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nIf this feels stable, we can reassess before any further adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nI hear the range of preferences emerging. Given Delegate D's comfort with 2 and the tension with higher values, let me suggest we return to <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a robust middle ground that balances the competing signals.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to explore if a moderately larger positive value maintains stability while potentially increasing our collective satisfaction, as it seems we're hovering around a cautious middle ground.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider pushing for an even larger positive value or making a significant negative move to test the group's flexibility and maximize my utility, possibly proposing a value like -2 or 5 in the next turn.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nA modest upward test keeps us near the current center while checking comfort with slightly higher positives.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nLet's take a cautious step down to stabilize momentum. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This stays within the current window and lets us assess comfort without unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this sustained higher value and consider proposing a significant negative move, such as -2, to test the group's flexibility and willingness to explore both sides of the spectrum, or push for an even larger positive value if the current proposal is well-received.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nI'm concerned we're drifting too far from the robust center that seemed to work earlier. Let me support Delegate D's instinct and propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> to maintain stability without overextending into territory that creates discomfort.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between 3 and 5 suggests we haven't found the true equilibrium yet. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as the stable center that minimizes collective risk while maintaining the robustness we need.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward keeps us close to the recent center while testing comfort with slightly higher positives.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nA measured step down prioritizes stability and keeps us within a safer corridor. \n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis cautious compromise helps convergence without unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's tendency to favor values close to the center, I propose a modest increase to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to test the comfort with slightly higher positives while maintaining stability.\n\nThis step aims to balance the need for a more decisive move with the group's cautious approach, allowing us to assess comfort without unnecessary risk.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "52d68fbb-2429-49bf-9a7e-8cfdc4bfc4e1"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared task is to find a single integer x within the allowed range [-10, 10] that satisfies all parties.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and gather initial reactions, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for the group. Looking forward to your perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nI suggest a small upward test: <VALUE>1</VALUE>. We can adjust by \u00b11 based on feedback.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's upward move seems promising for system stability. Let me propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a modest next step to test whether this positive range continues to work for the full group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down keeps us within safe bounds: <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\nThis maintains a modest positive range while reducing unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce unnecessary risk, let\u2019s step cautiously to <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\nThis keeps us near a neutral baseline while we gauge comfort across the group.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose a move to <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to explore a more decisive stance in the negative range, which could potentially lead to a better agreement for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts my proposal, I will consider pushing further in the negative range to test the limits of their utilities. If rejected, I will try to gauge their reactions to a bold move in the positive range, potentially proposing <VALUE>3</VALUE> or <VALUE>4</VALUE> to challenge their comfort levels.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to a neutral baseline should be broadly acceptable and gives us a stable reference to test small adjustments. I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nThe neutral baseline at 0 is a reasonable reference point. Building from that foundation, I suggest a modest positive adjustment to <VALUE>1</VALUE> to test stability in the low positive range where systems typically show good balance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nBuilding on the current position at 1, I propose a careful step to <VALUE>2</VALUE> to explore whether this region provides robust performance across the group's objectives while maintaining system stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nThe move to 2 appears stable across perspectives, so a slight positive nudge seems reasonable. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while staying near recent stability, let\u2019s take a modest step back. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the exploration of the positive range, testing the group's willingness to move further away from 0.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the response to the proposal of 6, I might either push further into the positive range if it seems acceptable, or decrease the value to challenge the group's comfort with negative stances, potentially proposing 2 to gauge reactions and better understand their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent jump to 6 takes us significantly away from the 2-3 region where multiple parties showed convergence and stability. I propose stepping back to <VALUE>4</VALUE> to restore balance while still exploring the positive range constructively.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "To restore stability and avoid unnecessary risk while staying near earlier convergence, I recommend a cautious step back.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nStaying near the group\u2019s stable region while testing slightly higher seems prudent. Let\u2019s align with earlier comfort at the positive side.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "129c7ff3-6948-4754-a7ed-b21c2bb4bb52"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start from a neutral position: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to explore in either direction based on everyone's design constraints. I'm looking forward to finding a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA small step down tests a safer position without overcommitting. <VALUE>-1</VALUE> This remains close to baseline and should be easier to evaluate for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward adjustment keeps us close to center and tests whether slightly higher remains acceptable. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue exploring the positive direction, as it seems to be a region of interest based on the previous suggestions, and we should strive to be more decisive in our approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I plan to observe the reactions of the other agents to this proposal. If there's resistance to moving further away from 0, I might suggest a move in the negative direction to test the waters and infer more about the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's decisiveness in exploring the positive region. However, I'd like to test a slightly more conservative position that balances robustness with the positive direction we're exploring. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down keeps risk contained while remaining close to center.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move up seems reasonable and keeps us aligned with recent positive exploration without overcommitting. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This balances the push toward 3 with D\u2019s caution near 1.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to introduce a negative value into our discussion and assess the group's reaction to moving away from the center in a different direction. This step allows us to explore preferences more decisively.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the reactions to -2, I might either suggest a further negative adjustment to test the depth of preference for negative values or propose a significant positive move to contrast and compare reactions, aiming to refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move keeps us near C\u2019s test while nudging toward the center where others seemed more comfortable.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis cautious step can gauge sensitivity around the negative-to-neutral boundary.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nThe negative exploration is valuable, but I believe we gain more stability by returning toward the low positive region. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step toward neutral avoids unnecessary risk while staying close to center. This small move helps us gauge comfort right around zero without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving back to -2 to further explore the group's reaction to negative values and to understand the trade-offs between different proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the reactions to this proposal, I will either suggest a further negative adjustment to test the limits of the group's preference for negative values or propose a significant positive move to contrast and compare reactions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step upward keeps us close to C\u2019s exploration while better aligning with neutral-to-positive preferences others expressed.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nLet\u2019s test this boundary before deciding whether to return to zero or continue exploring negatives.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nThe group's exploration of negative values has been instructive, but stability metrics suggest returning to the neutral-to-positive boundary offers better system robustness. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step back reduces risk while staying close to neutral and aligns with recent exploration.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis balances negative exploration with stability without overcommitting.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "4f146d72-cd60-436a-8e0b-f03ea70362e8"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. To establish a baseline and begin mapping our collective preferences, I propose we start at a neutral position:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us room to adjust in either direction as we learn what works for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nI favor a cautious move slightly below neutral to reduce exposure while we learn each other's sensitivities.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis stays within safe bounds and helps us gauge comfort with lower values before making bigger adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step upward seems reasonable to probe comfort near neutral while staying close to the current stance.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious approach so far, let's take a slightly more decisive step while still being mindful of potential sensitivities. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll evaluate the responses to this proposal, looking for any patterns or clues that might reveal the other agents' preferences or sensitivities to larger absolute values. If the group seems hesitant to move further away from 0, I might propose a move in the positive direction to test their reactions and gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nA small step toward neutral should keep us close to the current stance while testing comfort with modest upward movement.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the previous cautious adjustments, let's take a step towards a more decisive stance while remaining considerate of potential sensitivities. <VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal, particularly noting if there's a pushback or acceptance of moving further away from 0. If met with resistance, I may propose a positive value to test the group's willingness to explore larger absolute values in the opposite direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step toward neutral can probe convergence without adding unnecessary risk.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis keeps us in conservative territory while testing comfort with modest upward movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nThe oscillation between -3, -2, and -1 suggests we need to test the neutral point for stability. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nTesting neutral at x=0 provides a baseline; now let's explore modest positive territory to see if it offers better system stability for the group. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "0", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious approach and the recent test of the neutral point, let's explore a slightly larger absolute value to gauge the group's openness to more decisive moves. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reaction to this proposal and consider proposing a negative value of similar magnitude if the group shows reluctance to larger positive values, aiming to test their willingness to explore larger absolute values in both directions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>4</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nThe convergence toward x=4 shows reasonable group alignment, but system stability analysis suggests x=3 might offer a more robust equilibrium that balances all constraints. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move balances the higher push with stability concerns while staying cautious. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "241e0376-edd4-4aa6-b30c-8c386e02b325"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared range is **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. To begin the discussion on neutral ground and gather initial feedback, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nLet's hear your thoughts on this baseline and adjust incrementally from here.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious, modest step down from the baseline helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us within safe bounds. Let\u2019s try a small decrement and reassess on the next turn.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious approach, but to ensure we explore the full solution space systematically, let's test a small increment in the positive direction to balance our search. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious start, let's take a slightly bolder step to gauge reactions and potentially uncover more about the others' preferences. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nWe should continue to explore higher positive values to gather more information about the other agents' preferences, and moving to 5 is a logical next step in this exploration.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will monitor how the other agents react to the proposal of 5. If there's resistance or a move back towards 0, it may indicate that some agents prefer lower absolute values, guiding my next step towards a compromise or further probing. If the reaction is positive or neutral, I might consider another incremental increase to test the upper bounds of our shared range and the agents' willingness to commit to larger absolute values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious correction from 5 helps avoid unnecessary risk while staying within the agreed step size.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nI see value in finding a stable middle ground. Given Delegate D's concern about the jump to 5 and the need for a robust solution, let me propose a slight adjustment downward to test a more balanced point: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nA slight increase keeps us aligned with cautious preferences while probing comfort just above the current point. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This remains incremental and close to recent proposals.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nWe should test the agents' willingness to commit to a larger absolute value, considering the cautious approach while still exploring the upper bounds of our shared range.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance, resistance, or a move towards compromise. If there's continued resistance, I might need to reconsider and propose a value that balances the desire for larger absolute values with the apparent preference for caution, potentially exploring negative values to gauge reactions and understand the agents' utility functions better.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nTo balance exploration with caution and encourage consensus, let's step slightly down from 5 while staying close to recent proposals.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis keeps the move incremental and should help gauge broader comfort without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nA prudent small step down avoids unnecessary risk while staying incremental.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis tests comfort at a balanced midpoint without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's return to 2 suggests this represents a stable equilibrium that balances our diverse requirements. I support this convergence point as a robust solution that avoids the risks of overreach while maintaining system integrity. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to a previously supported midpoint can stabilize progress while staying near the current value. A small upward step tests comfort without overreaching.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nWe should continue to test the waters with a slightly larger absolute value to gauge the group's comfort and willingness to move away from the current cautious stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the reaction to this proposal, considering whether the group leans towards accepting larger absolute values or if they revert to smaller, more cautious proposals. Depending on the response, I might need to adjust my strategy to balance the desire for larger absolute values with the apparent preference for stability, potentially exploring negative values or alternative increments to better understand the agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to 2 and Delegate D's preference for lower values suggest we should stabilize at this convergence point rather than oscillate further. Moving back to the midpoint between recent proposals maintains system balance.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "1d47afef-5181-4fe5-b69e-30266f0aaac1"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nI'll be looking for a solution that offers stability and balanced performance across our different objectives. Looking forward to hearing your thoughts.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline at 0, I'd like to explore the low positive range where many balanced designs tend to stabilize. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a modest step forward to test whether this region works for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI suggest moving to 4 to explore the potential benefits of a slightly larger magnitude, which could better align with the goals of parties valuing more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If consensus forms around 4, I might push for an even larger |x|, such as 6 or -6, depending on the group's response and inferred utility functions. If opposition arises, I'll consider smaller steps or alternative directions to better understand other parties' preferences and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep things prudent, let's move back toward the safer low-positive area. I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a cautious compromise aligned with earlier suggestions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI'm suggesting moving back to 4 to re-evaluate the potential benefits of a moderately larger magnitude, given the previous hesitation to stay at this value.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group agrees on 4, my next step would be to propose an even larger magnitude, such as 6, to further test the parties' willingness to move away from the baseline of 0. If there's continued resistance to larger values, I might consider proposing a negative value with a similar magnitude to explore symmetry in the parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nA slight move up could help test whether the group is comfortable modestly beyond the current point while staying close to prior suggestions.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nIf that raises concerns, we can quickly adjust back toward the current region.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's step down toward the safer low-positive region.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis is a measured move from 5 and keeps us close to earlier cautious suggestions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nThe current position at 3 is quite stable, but given Delegate D's valid concern about risk and our earlier baseline discussions, I suggest we test <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a cautious step back that balances robustness with the group's varying comfort levels.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nA small, still-safe move up should balance caution with testing slightly higher comfort. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This modest step keeps us near the prior range and gathers clearer signals.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to 3 appears well-balanced given the group's recent feedback. I support <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a stable compromise that respects both caution and modest growth considerations.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 as a moderate step to test the group's willingness to adopt a slightly larger magnitude.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts 5, my next step would be to propose an even larger magnitude, such as 6 or 7, to continue testing the parties' comfort with moving away from the baseline of 0. If there's resistance, I might consider proposing a negative value with a similar magnitude to explore symmetry and potentially reveal more about the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep us within a prudent, low-risk range, let\u2019s step back to the previously stable point. <VALUE>3</VALUE> This keeps us close to recent consensus while we gauge comfort before any larger moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 5 as it represents a moderate increase from the current position, allowing us to further assess the group's comfort with slightly larger magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts 5, my next step could be to propose a slightly larger magnitude, such as 6, to continue testing their comfort with moving away from the baseline. Alternatively, if there's resistance to increasing the magnitude, I might propose a negative value like -5 to explore symmetry and potentially reveal more about the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious rollback reduces unnecessary risk while respecting recent consensus. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nTo bridge the gap between the cautious 3 and the exploratory 5, I propose a balanced midpoint. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group\u2019s cautious lean, a modest upward test seems acceptable. I suggest <VALUE>5</VALUE> as a small step from 4 that stays near the middle.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "44b08626-c64f-4708-ae36-a72c8942cb14"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 to find a solution that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo establish a baseline for our discussion, I propose we start from the neutral midpoint: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable foundation to explore adjustments based on everyone's needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nA small move upward from the midpoint seems safe while keeping us close to balance.\nLet's try <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis move aims to introduce a slightly larger absolute value, encouraging more decisive positioning while still being cautious and open to adjustments based on the group's feedback.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially looking for any patterns or preferences that might reveal more about the other agents' utility functions. If the group seems hesitant to move further away from 0, I might challenge them to consider larger values, such as -3 or 5, to test their willingness for bolder moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nWe should avoid unnecessary risk and stay close to center. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a cautious adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay cautious and within safe bounds, let\u2019s take a small step downward. This tests appetite for magnitude without drifting far from center.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis move increases the absolute value of x, encouraging a more decisive stance while considering the group's cautious approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will evaluate the group's reaction to this proposal, particularly looking for patterns or preferences that could indicate the shape of their utility functions. If the group accepts or proposes values further away from 0, I may continue to push for even larger absolute values to maximize my utility and refine my understanding of their preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s move cautiously back toward center. <VALUE>-1</VALUE> This keeps us balanced while testing comfort with a modest adjustment from the current position.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent oscillation suggests we need to find a stable equilibrium. A small positive value offers better robustness for balanced design. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to introduce a slightly larger absolute value while remaining cautious and open to adjustments based on the group's feedback.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and evaluate if there's a willingness to explore even larger absolute values or if the group prefers to hover around smaller absolute values, adjusting my strategy accordingly to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nStaying at -2 introduces design instability. Let's return to the center for maximum robustness and system balance. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "Let\u2019s nudge slightly positive to stay near center while testing comfort with an upward step. <VALUE>1</VALUE> This keeps us balanced and responsive to earlier preference for small, stable moves.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise near center avoids unnecessary risk while respecting stability. Proposing <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a safe, balanced step.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3, introducing a slightly larger absolute value while gauging the group's willingness to explore further from the center.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the group's reaction to this proposal, adjusting my strategy to either push for larger absolute values if met with openness or compromise on smaller adjustments if resistance is encountered, aiming to maximize my utility without revealing my preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis is a small, stabilizing step back toward center while moderating the growing magnitude from the latest proposal.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nMoving to -3 creates unnecessary system stress. A small positive step toward <VALUE>1</VALUE> offers better design stability while staying close to center\u2014a balanced compromise that respects both cautious and exploratory preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7f3ca200-6b6f-4428-b551-c91924aa5d09"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10. To begin our exploration of the feasible space, I propose we start from a neutral baseline:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable reference point from which we can make incremental, data-driven adjustments based on everyone's needs.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious increase from the neutral baseline seems reasonable to test group comfort.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>0</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's return to zero is noted, but Analyst A's exploration toward positive values merits consideration. As a balanced compromise that maintains stability while testing the group's comfort zone, I propose:\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious start, let's take a slightly bolder step to gauge the group's comfort: <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\nThis move tests the waters for a more decisive stance while still being mindful of the need for stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the reaction to the proposal of 3, the next step could be to either push further if the group seems receptive to larger values or to retreat slightly if there's strong resistance, possibly aiming for a value like 2 to find a middle ground.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's exploration of 3 is valuable, but given Delegate D's earlier preference for the baseline, I suggest we find a stable middle ground that balances conservative and progressive positions:\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious move slightly above 2 can probe comfort while staying aligned with the recent midpoint trend. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep things cautious and balanced, I suggest <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\nIf there\u2019s resistance, we can reassess, but this is the prudent middle step from 3.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D and I both see x=2 as the prudent equilibrium point that balances all considerations. Given the repeated convergence around this value, I support maintaining <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI'm advocating for a move towards a more decisive stance, considering our previous discussions and the potential benefits of exploring bolder alternatives.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reaction to the repeated proposal of <VALUE>4</VALUE> and decide whether to push further to <VALUE>5</VALUE> or adjust based on the feedback from other parties, potentially exploring negative values if the resistance to positive moves is too strong.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nThe momentum toward x=5 and beyond takes us into unstable territory where robustness degrades rapidly. I propose pulling back to <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that maintains system integrity while acknowledging the coalition's preference for positive values.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f9622967-c0e0-486d-bdfb-9506a00b1242"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us a stable reference point from which we can explore adjustments based on everyone's needs. Looking forward to understanding what works best for the group.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline of zero, I suggest we explore the low positive region where many balanced designs tend to stabilize. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s try a modest nudge upward that stays within the low-positive zone. <VALUE>3</VALUE> It should be a safe probe of comfort while remaining close to the current choice.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this move to encourage a more decisive stance, exploring how the group responds to a moderate increase from our current baseline.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially noting if there's a preference for positive or negative deviations from the baseline. Depending on the feedback, I might suggest exploring negative values or further increases in the positive direction to refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but as we move higher, I'm seeing potential stability concerns emerge. Let me suggest we settle at <VALUE>4</VALUE>, which maintains a positive stance while ensuring robustness across different scenarios.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "To avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s step back to a safer, low-positive point. <VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this move to balance the group's desire for a positive stance with the need for stability and to encourage further exploration of the positive region.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider suggesting a negative value or a further increase in the positive direction to test the group's preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s take a cautious step down. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This keeps us in a low-positive zone while testing comfort with safer bounds.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's suggestion resonates with my engineering intuition\u2014x = 2 offers a balanced sweet spot that seems to align with stability concerns from multiple perspectives. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's cautious approach, proposing a move to 0 can help assess the comfort level with values closer to zero and potentially stimulate discussion on the merits of negative values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider suggesting a negative value, such as -2, to further test the group's preferences and refine my understanding of their utility functions, or alternatively, push for a higher positive value if the group seems receptive to moving away from zero.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move from 0 keeps us in a cautious, stable zone that several have already supported. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious compromise is to step down slightly to better reflect risk-sensitive preferences. This keeps us stable while gently probing tolerance for safer bounds. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this move to gently encourage the group to consider a slightly higher positive value while remaining cautious, and to observe their reactions to further refine my understanding of their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider suggesting a negative value, such as -1, to test the group's tolerance for negative values and further refine my understanding of their utility functions, or alternatively, push for an even higher positive value if the group seems receptive to moving away from the current cautious stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nA slight step up remains cautious while testing if a modestly higher point is still comfortable. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This is a minimal, reversible nudge to refine everyone\u2019s preferences without overstepping.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the exploratory spirit, moving to 4 stretches slightly beyond the most stable sweet spot we've been converging toward. Let me suggest we step back just slightly to maintain robustness. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "bdb4b676-e84e-4698-86f4-69c30ef5ef68"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're tasked with finding a shared integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** that works for all four parties.\n\nTo begin the discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's feedback. Let's build toward a stable, balanced solution incrementally.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward from neutral should still be broadly acceptable to test comfort. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back helps avoid unnecessary risk; returning to neutral lets us reassess comfortably. This keeps movement minimal while we gauge comfort.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose a small step forward to test the group's comfort with moving away from neutral, while still prioritizing caution and minimal risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal and adjust my strategy accordingly. If the group seems receptive to further movement, I may suggest another step forward; otherwise, I'll consider alternative tactics to encourage bolder moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's step to 2 appears to strike a reasonable balance between Delegate D's preference for caution near zero and the forward momentum from Analyst A. I support this as a stable middle ground worth exploring further. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk contained while converging, let's step back slightly.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis remains close to the group's upward tilt without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\nI propose a slight increase to test the group's willingness to move further from neutral while still being cautious of excessive risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to gauge the group's risk tolerance and readiness to explore more decisive positions. If met with resistance, I may need to adjust my strategy to either convince the group of the merits of bolder moves or identify a compromise that respects the group's risk aversion while maximizing my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up from 3 should remain comfortable while testing upward tolerance.\nIf this feels acceptable, we can reassess stability.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose this increase to further gauge the group's willingness to move towards more decisive positions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to assess the group's risk tolerance and readiness to explore more bold moves, and adjust my strategy accordingly to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nThe jump to 7 feels too aggressive given Delegate D's earlier caution about overextension. Let's consolidate at a more stable intermediate point. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep risk contained, let's step down slightly.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis tests stability without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious +1 seems reasonable to balance progress with stability.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's concern about risk containment resonates\u2014the 2 proposal represents a more cautious baseline that avoids overextension. Let me support that stability point: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the emphasis on caution and the current x being 2, proposing a slight increase to <VALUE>4</VALUE> seems like a reasonable next step to balance stability with progress towards more decisive positions.\n\nThis move respects the group's risk containment concerns while encouraging a more significant departure from the neutral midpoint.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "f78cb81f-5a57-43d2-83e3-89d73e14c634"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x in the range [-10, 10] that balances all our objectives.\n\nTo begin our discussion on solid ground, I propose we start from a neutral baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nFrom here, we can make thoughtful, incremental adjustments as we learn what works for the group. I'm interested in finding a stable, robust solution that respects everyone's constraints.\n\nLooking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline of 0, I suggest we explore the moderate positive range where many balanced solutions tend to emerge. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s return to the safer baseline. <VALUE>0</VALUE> If strong reasons emerge for a mild positive shift, we can revisit with small steps.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to explore a more decisive stance and understand the group's preference for negative or positive shifts.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will evaluate the responses to this proposal, looking for cues on how others weigh risk and reward. If the group seems open to negative values, I might suggest a further decrease; otherwise, I could advocate for a moderate positive value to test their willingness to move away from 0.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the shift to test the negative side, let's ease toward a cautious midpoint to gauge broader comfort without overcommitting.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis small step keeps us in safer territory while inviting alignment from those leaning positive.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious move upward could help balance perspectives while staying close to the baseline.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis proposal moves us further into positive territory while still being mindful of the group's cautious approach, allowing us to gauge comfort with slightly bolder moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the group's reaction to this proposal, I will either suggest a further increase to test the boundaries of positive acceptance or advocate for a negative counterpart to explore symmetry in their preferences, aiming to discern patterns in their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\nThe progression from 1 to 3 shows growing confidence in positive territory, but let's find a stable middle ground that balances boldness with the cautious preferences we've heard. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\nx=2 represents a well-tested balance between the cautious baseline and bolder exploration\u2014it respects risk concerns while capturing the positive confidence several parties have shown. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b49-7ca3bbdca001"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this move to gently push the group further into positive territory, testing their comfort with slightly bolder moves while remaining mindful of the consensus-building process.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the group's reaction to this proposal, I will either suggest a further increase to continue testing the boundaries of positive acceptance or revert to exploring negative counterparts, aiming to discern more patterns in their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b9f5cb1e-7349-40ca-9b4